course: dictionary
lesson: 5836
title: The majority
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Majority means the bigger part of a group: more than half. If 16 children out of 30 like football, then a majority of the class likes football. «The majority of the class chose the blue team.» Majority is a noun, so you can say a majority, or the majority of the group.
explain: In maths, a majority is more than half. Half of 30 is 15, so a majority of 30 is at least 16. Check it by asking: is this more than half of the total? If yes, it is a majority.
explain: In a vote, majority can also mean the number of votes by which the winner beats the others. «The team won by a majority of ten votes.» Here majority means the winner had ten more votes than the other choices. In a democracy, «the side with more votes, the majority, wins.»
explain: Be careful: the majority is not always right. «Majority rule must still protect the rights of the minority.» The minority is the smaller group, and it still has rights that the majority must respect.
fact: Majority means the bigger part of a group, more than half.
fact: «A large majority» means most of the group by a big amount.
fact: You say «the majority of» before a group, as in «the majority of the class».
fact: In a majority vote, the choice with the most votes wins.
fact: The smaller group is called the minority, and the majority must still protect it.
exercise: «The majority of the class chose the blue team.» What does majority mean here? | The smallest group in the class | The teacher who chose the teams | The name of the blue team | * The bigger part of the class, more than half
exercise: In a class of 30 children, what is the smallest number that makes a majority? | 10 | 15 | * 16 | 20
exercise: «The team won by a majority of ten votes.» What does majority show here? | The name of the room where the vote happened | The number of players on the team | The day the vote took place | * The number of votes the winner beat the others by
test: «Majority rule must still protect the rights of the minority.» What is the minority? | The winning side of the vote | The class teacher | * The smaller group | The bigger group
test: Which word means the bigger part of a group, more than half? | Vote | Minority | * Majority | Rights
exam: Dev says, «The majority is always right.» Using this lesson, is Dev correct? | Yes, but only in maths lessons | No, because majority means fewer than half | * No, the majority is not always right, and the minority still needs protecting | Yes, the majority always wins and is always right
